          "type": "text",
          "text": "\n\nExcellent! All tests pass. Let me create a quick documentation of the changes:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully extended the TIFF export configuration with four new fields to support pyramidal layers and tiled storage. Here are the changes:\n\n### Changes Made\n\n**1. `/workspace/vips/image.go`** - Extended `TiffExportParams` struct:\n   - Added `Pyramid bool` - enables multi-resolution pyramid TIFF\n   - Added `Tile bool` - enables tiled storage\n   - Added `TileWidth int` - tile width in pixels (default: 256)\n   - Added `TileHeight int` - tile height in pixels (default: 256)\n\n**2. `/workspace/vips/foreign.go`** - Updated `vipsSaveTIFFToBuffer()`:\n   - Now passes all new parameters to the C layer\n   - Also ensures `Predictor` is properly passed (was missing before)\n\n**3. `/workspace/examples/tiff/example_tiff_image.go`** - Updated example:\n   - Demonstrates usage of the new pyramid and tile features\n\n### API Usage\n\n```go\n// Default behavior (backward compatible - no pyramid, no tile)\nparams := vips.NewTiffExportParams()\n// Pyramid=false, Tile=false, TileWidth=256, TileHeight=256\n\n// Enable pyramidal TIFF for deep-zoom viewers\nparams.Pyramid = true\n\n// Enable tiled storage for efficient region reads\nparams.Tile = true\nparams.TileWidth = 512\nparams.TileHeight = 512\n\n// Export with all settings\nimageBytes, _, err := img.ExportTiff(params)\n```\n\n### Defaults\n- `Pyramid`: `false` (preserves existing behavior)\n- `Tile`: `false` (preserves existing behavior)\n- `TileWidth`: `256` (sensible default for when tiling is enabled)\n- `TileHeight`: `256` (sensible default for when tiling is enabled)\n\nThe implementation leverages the existing libvips support that was already present in the C layer but not exposed through the Go API. All existing tests pass, confirming backward compatibility.",
